{{/*
  Ticket template. Go text/template over pkg/ticket.TemplateData.

  The FIRST line must be "Summary: ..."; then a blank line; then the description
  body. Keeping both in one file means the whole wording of a ticket lives in one
  place, editable by whoever owns the process rather than in Go.

  Available:
    .ServiceName .Images .ImageCount .GroupNoun .Refs .Priority
    .Source .SourcePath - the shared change target, present on grouped tickets too
    .Accounts .Namespaces .Teams .WorkloadCount
    .CriticalCount .HighCount .ProviderAssessed
    .FixableCriticals (.ID .CVSS .EPSS .FixedVersion .KEV) .MaxEPSS .KnownExploited
    .Urgent   - the CVEs the proposed change was measured to clear (exploited,
                or EPSS at or above jira.urgentEPSS, with a fix), each with .Why
                .Where .Action .Package .FixedVersion .Reference. ONLY what the
                change clears: empty when nothing was measured, which is not a
                claim that it clears nothing
    .UrgentCleared .UrgentUnknown .UrgentRemaining .UrgentAllCleared - kept
                for older templates; with .Urgent holding only cleared CVEs
                they are len(.Urgent), 0, 0 and "non-empty"
    .Upgrade  - the single version move, or NIL when the grouped images do not
                share one target version (.Kind .Name .Current .Latest .Managed
                .Source .SourcePath .Direct)
    .Fixes    - images updated as a CONSEQUENCE of .Upgrades, not work in
                themselves (chain-merged tickets only)
    .Upgrades - the version move(s) to apply, one entry per image the change
                moves (.Ref .Repo .Current .Latest .Source .SourcePath .Managed
                .Direct). .Current/.Latest are the image's own tags; when a Helm
                chart owns the version, .Chart .ChartCurrent .ChartLatest name it,
                and .Latest is empty if the target chart's tag could not be read
    .Disambiguator - set ONLY when another ticket in this run renders the same
                summary, naming what makes this one different. Empty otherwise,
                so putting it in a summary costs nothing on the tickets that
                have nothing to be confused with.

  This is an EXAMPLE. Edit it to match how your teams actually work.
*/ -}}
{{- if .Upgrade -}}
Summary: Upgrade {{ .ServiceName }} to {{ .Upgrade.Latest }}{{ with .Disambiguator }} ({{ . }}){{ end }}
{{- else -}}
Summary: Upgrade {{ .ServiceName }} {{ .GroupNoun }} ({{ .ImageCount }}) to their latest versions{{ with .Disambiguator }} ({{ . }}){{ end }}
{{- end }}

**Business objective/requirements**

{{ if .Upgrade -}}
Upgrade {{ .ServiceName }} from {{ .Upgrade.Current }} to {{ .Upgrade.Latest }} to clear known container vulnerabilities.
{{- else -}}
Upgrade the {{ .ImageCount }} images below to clear known container vulnerabilities. {{ if .Source }}They are grouped because one change covers them all.{{ else }}They are grouped because they are managed together; each is bumped in its own place, listed below.{{ end }}
{{- end }}

**Technical Requirements & Actions**

{{ range .Upgrades }}* {{ .Repo }}: {{ if .Chart }}{{ .Current }}{{ if .Latest }} -> {{ .Latest }}{{ end }} (set by the {{ .Chart }} chart, which moves {{ .ChartCurrent }} -> {{ .ChartLatest }}{{ if not .Latest }}; the tag it deploys could not be read, so check it after the upgrade{{ end }}){{ else }}{{ .Current }} -> {{ .Latest }}{{ end }}{{ if not .Direct }} ({{ if eq .Managed "helm" }}version owned by its Helm chart, so bump it there{{ else }}version owned by the {{ .Managed }}, so bump it there{{ end }}){{ end }}{{ if and (not $.Source) .Source }}, change in {{ .Source }}{{ if .SourcePath }} path {{ .SourcePath }}{{ end }}{{ end }}
{{ end -}}
{{- with .Fixes }}
This also updates the following, which are not bumped directly:

{{ range . }}* {{ .Repo }}: {{ .Current }}{{ if .Latest }} -> {{ .Latest }}{{ end }}
{{ end -}}
{{- end }}
{{- if and .Upgrade (eq .Upgrade.Kind "base") }}* Rebuild {{ .ServiceName }}: it is built on top of {{ .Upgrade.Name }}, and moving that to {{ .Upgrade.Latest }} is what the rebuild picks up.{{ if .Urgent }} That alone clears every CVE under "Done means".{{ end }}
{{ if .BuildRepo }}* Rebuild from {{ .BuildRepo }}.
{{ end }}* Redeploy the new image everywhere it runs, listed below. A rebuilt image fixes nothing until it is running.
{{ else }}{{- if .Source }}* Change target: {{ .Source }}{{ if .SourcePath }} (path: {{ .SourcePath }}){{ end }}
{{ end }}{{ end }}
{{ with .Urgent -}}
